\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.asymptote_factor_certificate}
The hyperbola $\varepsilon^2 = 49/4$ makes the scattering asymptote factor
$1/\sqrt{\varepsilon^2 - 1} = 1/\sqrt{49/4 - 1} = 2/\sqrt{45}$.
(Iter-014 repair: previously the false $67/4$, $2/\sqrt{63}$ pair.)
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
$49/4 - 1 = 45/4 = (\sqrt{45}/2)^2$ using $\sqrt{45}^{\,2} = 45$; taking
the positive square root gives $\sqrt{45/4} = \sqrt{45}/2$, and inverting
yields $2/\sqrt{45}$.  Pure algebra up to that square-root identity.
\end{proof}

